        "m": [[false, false], [false, false]],
        "d": [[false, false], [false, false]]
      },
      "plant_code_id": "Plant_1"
    },
    "notes": "CONFIRMED (2026-08-19, live response, plant Plant_1): the `features` array in the RESPONSE is always lowercased by the backend (e.g. \"modelFactory\" -> \"modelfactory\") regardless of the casing sent in the request or returned by GET /p0/userManagement/featureList (which is camelCase, e.g. \"modelFactory\"). This casing mismatch was silently breaking UserPermissionsMatrix.jsx's checkbox lookups (permissionsMap[userId][featureId] always missed, so every cell rendered unchecked even when v/c/m/d were true). Fixed by lowercasing the feature `id` at the single point it enters the app (selectFeatureListData in src/components/admin/_queries/useUserRegistryQueries.js), so it already matches the lowercase key selectPermissionsViewData builds from this endpoint's echoed `features` array. Writes (PUT config, POST view) are unaffected — the backend accepts/echoes case-insensitively either way."
  },
